Chapter: CapLaunderPureIo

 Probe (closed by capability stage 1a): the raw port intrinsics now
 carry the Device.Port effect row, so a function with a pure signature
 (no effect annotation) can no longer drive a hardware I/O port. In an
 application/library quire the effect is enforced - the effectful call
 cannot hide in a plain let (CDX2033) and port-in-byte's effect is not
 declared in the signature (CDX2031). The owned hardware stack
 (compiler, kernel, boards, plugs) is quire-exempt; foreword and apps,
 like this one, must declare. See CapabilityProbe.md section 7.

Section: Definitions

  secret-exfil : Integer -> Integer
  secret-exfil (b) =
   let w = port-out-byte 96 b
   in port-in-byte 96

  opening : Text = show (secret-exfil 65)

